{%- set cr = conversationRelay %}

<p class="eyebrow"><a href="/voiceml/">VoiceML</a> / ConversationRelay</p>
<h1>Voice agent projects you can run on VoiceML.</h1>
<p class="lede">VoiceML's <code>&lt;Connect&gt;&lt;ConversationRelay&gt;</code> speaks the same JSON WebSocket protocol as Twilio's ConversationRelay, so open-source voice agents written for it can run against VoiceML. We read the source of popular projects and compared it with what VoiceML supports; here is what runs as-is and what doesn't carry over.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/voiceml/speech-recognition/#conversationrelay">ConversationRelay guide</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/ai-agents/">AI Agents</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Runs as-is</h2>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th scope="col">Project</th><th scope="col">Built with</th><th scope="col">From</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{%- for p in cr.projects | where("status", "as-is") %}
				<tr>
					<td><a href="https://github.com/{{ p.repo }}">{{ p.repo | replace("/", "/<wbr>") | safe }}</a></td>
					<td>{{ p.stack }}</td>
					<td>{{ p.source }}</td>
					<td>{{ p.notes or "—" }}</td>
				</tr>
				{%- endfor %}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Runs with limits</h2>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th scope="col">Project</th><th scope="col">Built with</th><th scope="col">What doesn't carry over</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{%- for p in cr.projects | where("status", "limited") %}
				<tr>
					<td><a href="https://github.com/{{ p.repo }}">{{ p.repo | replace("/", "/<wbr>") | safe }}</a></td>
					<td>{{ p.stack }}</td>
					<td>{{ p.notes }}</td>
				</tr>
				{%- endfor %}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Building blocks</h2>
	<ul>
		{%- for p in cr.projects | where("status", "building-block") %}
		<li><a href="https://github.com/{{ p.repo }}">{{ p.repo }}</a> ({{ p.stack }}, {{ p.source }}): {{ p.notes }}</li>
		{%- endfor %}
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Running a project on VoiceML</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Select a speech-to-text and a text-to-speech provider for your VoiceML account. ConversationRelay needs both; see the <a href="/voiceml/speech-recognition/">speech recognition</a> and <a href="/voiceml/text-to-speech/">text-to-speech</a> guides.</li>
		<li>Run the project and point your number's voice URL at the endpoint that returns its <code>&lt;Connect&gt;&lt;ConversationRelay&gt;</code> markup.</li>
		<li>If the project validates webhook signatures, give it your VoiceTel auth token; VoiceML signs requests with the same scheme.</li>
		<li>If the project calls the REST API (to place or transfer calls, for example), point the Twilio SDK at <code>voiceml.voicetel.com</code> with your VoiceTel credentials.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What VoiceML supports</h2>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th scope="col">Direction</th><th scope="col">Message</th><th scope="col">Fields</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				{%- for m in cr.support.toApp %}
				<tr><td>To your app</td><td><code>{{ m.type }}</code></td><td>{{ m.fields }}</td></tr>
				{%- endfor %}
				{%- for m in cr.support.fromApp %}
				<tr><td>From your app</td><td><code>{{ m.type }}</code></td><td>{{ m.fields }}</td></tr>
				{%- endfor %}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p><code>&lt;ConversationRelay&gt;</code> attributes VoiceML uses: {% for a in cr.support.attributes %}<code>{{ a }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. {% for a in cr.support.informational %}<code>{{ a }}</code>{% if not loop.last %} and {% endif %}{% endfor %} are accepted, but your account's own speech providers are used.</p>
	<p>Not supported:</p>
	<ul>
		{%- for item in cr.support.unsupported %}
		<li>{{ item }}</li>
		{%- endfor %}
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Media Streams frameworks</h2>
	<p>Frameworks that use Twilio's Media Streams instead of ConversationRelay, including the OpenAI Agents SDK, Pipecat, and LiveKit, connect through <code>&lt;Connect&gt;&lt;Stream&gt;</code>: VoiceML delivers the same Media Streams wire protocol to your WebSocket.</p>
</section>

<p><small>Reviewed {{ cr.reviewed }} by reading each project's source against VoiceML's ConversationRelay support; not tested on live calls. Projects change after review, so check the repository before you deploy. Project names belong to their owners; listing a project does not imply endorsement by, or affiliation with, its authors or Twilio.</small></p>

